<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 3 · Paper B · Learner paper · 繁體</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-3/b/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 3 Course Review · Original Paper B</p><h1>Learner paper · 繁體</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 90-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 3 B</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 25 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><p class="gloss">號碼: participant number</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. When did the speaker first help at the neighbourhood event?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 前年暑假開始後的第一個週六</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 去年暑假結束前的最後一天</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 今年開學後的第一個週六</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">主角: central figure</p><p class="gloss">相冊: photo album</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. Whom had the man originally regarded as the main people at the event?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 提前準備場地的人</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 等候比賽結果的鄰居</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 參加比賽的人</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why does he add the other photographs and names?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲他終於找到了自己領獎的照片</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 照片讓他注意到準備工作也支持了活動</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因爲媽媽要求他刪去全部比賽照片</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">思路: reasoning approach</p><p class="gloss">圈出來: circle/mark</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What help does the woman explicitly ask for?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 把每道題的最終答案發給她</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 替她完成還沒寫的全部步驟</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 解釋第二步的思路，不直接給最後答案</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What best explains the man’s final suggestion?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 認爲只有把整本練習都講完纔算幫助</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 兼顧她獨立思考的需要和今天有限的時間</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 準備從此不再討論這道題</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><p class="gloss">指示: directions/signs</p><p class="gloss">路線圖: route map</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What will the speaker do before the design activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先替社區安裝所有新的路牌</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 等活動結束後才第一次觀察路口</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 畫路線圖，請朋友試讀並記錄問題</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">模型: model</p><p class="gloss">上傳: upload</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What must participants prepare for Activity A?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一套自己購買的房屋模型材料</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 連續三天的同一盆植物記錄</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 活動結束後的三張合影</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which next step fits his interest, time and the instructions?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先做三天植物記錄，再上傳並等待甲的確認</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不做記錄，週六直接到甲活動現場</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 報名參加週日早上的模型活動</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">草稿: draft</p><p class="gloss">封面: cover</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Who is responsible for choosing quotations from the book?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 蘇芸</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 小杜</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 負責整理說明的女生</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. What arrangement have they agreed on?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 週二放學後所有人留下，一次完成整頁</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 午休共同確定和檢查，草稿各自在家準備</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 等小杜取消訓練後纔開始選書</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><p class="gloss">片段: extract/part</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What does this programme mainly offer?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 整本書逐字朗讀的完整錄音</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 按考試分數排列的必讀書名單</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 兩位讀者對同一本書不同片段的推薦</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">主角: main character</p><p class="gloss">告別: say goodbye</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How does Acheng’s approach to feedback change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 從自己寫故事，變爲讓朋友代寫全部內容</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 從喜歡原來的結尾，變爲刪去所有結尾</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 從只想查錯字，變爲願意聽問題並補充情節</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. What attitude is best supported by the final action?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 願意繼續聽意見，同時保留自己的判斷</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 以後別人提出的每個改法都必須照用</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只接受指出錯字、不涉及內容的意見</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">香草: herbs</p><p class="gloss">預約: reserve a place</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. What must a participant do before the afternoon activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 不預約，帶自己的土就能直接參加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上午先整理地面才能參加下午活動</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先預約；需要借盒子時一起說明</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which plan fits the man’s circumstances?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 確認下午名額，並在預約時提出借盒子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 爲了借盒子，改去自己沒空的上午活動</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先買土和工具，再認定下午肯定能參加</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><p class="gloss">澆水: water plants</p><p class="gloss">天氣預報: weather forecast</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. What is the revised meeting time?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 週日上午十一點</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週日早上八點</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 週六早上八點</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">畫具: drawing supplies</p><p class="gloss">從容: unhurried</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. How often is drawing scheduled in Xiaowen’s new weekday plan?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每個晚上連續畫一個半小時</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週一和週三晚飯後各半小時</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只在每天早上出門前畫十五分鐘</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. Which combination helps explain her less rushed preparation?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 完全停止畫畫，因此不再需要準備物品</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 堅持每天同一計劃，絕不因作業量改變</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 按時收好畫具，並把常用筆放在固定盒子裏</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">吉他: guitar</p><p class="gloss">完美: perfect</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. Which suggestion fits the woman’s available time and concern?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每次都熬夜完成整幅，纔算有進步</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每次練一個小部分，再留出休息時間</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先等到每天都有整晚空閒再開始</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. What changed view is supported by the man’s memory of the performance?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 他開始重視共同參與的經歷，而不只計算錯誤</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 他認定以後彈琴都不需要練習</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 他證明只要有朋友在場就絕不會忘曲子</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">整理抽屜時，我發現一張舊照片，背面寫着“三年前，秋天開學後的第二個週日”。那天社區第一次在小廣場放電影，我和鄰居一起把坐墊搬過去。電影的名字我已經記不清了，卻還記得散場後大家收東西時互相道謝。照片裏沒有銀幕，只有一排疊好的坐墊和幾個笑着的人。</p></div><p class="gloss">坐墊: seat cushion</p><p class="gloss">銀幕: cinema screen</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. When did the remembered community film event take place?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 三年前秋季開學後的第二個週日</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 三年前暑假開始後的第二個週六</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 去年秋天放假前的最後一個週日</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小時候，社區晚會結束後，我只想把自己唱歌的照片貼在牆上。我覺得那纔是值得讓朋友看的部分。上週整理舊相冊，我發現另一張照片：我還站在臺上，奶奶和幾個鄰居正在臺邊收線，兩個孩子幫着把空椅子放回屋裏。我當時一直等大人誇我的歌，沒有注意到他們。<br>後來我問奶奶，爲什麼她那天沒有一直坐着看。她說，中間下了一點雨，大家要把不用的東西先收好，晚會才能繼續。我再看自己唱歌的照片，旁邊已不是一些“不重要的人”。我請奶奶把他們的名字寫下來，準備下次見面時謝謝他們。</p></div><p class="gloss">收線: gather cables</p><p class="gloss">臺邊: beside the stage</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. Which photographs did the writer originally want to display?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 鄰居收好椅子的照片</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 自己唱歌的照片</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 奶奶寫下名字的照片</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why does the writer’s view of the people at the side change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 奶奶的解釋把收拾物品與晚會繼續聯繫起來</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 他們後來都上臺替作者唱完了歌曲</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 作者發現奶奶根本沒有參加那次晚會</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小寧：週五以前請把你負責的兩道例題說明發給我，我來整理成互助小組的複習頁。我們約好只寫解題理由，不放作業的完整答案。小博週四要訓練，週五午休才能檢查，所以請儘量別拖到最後。——小禾<br>小寧回覆：我能按時發，但第二道題還不太明白。我不想照抄網上的說明。今晚先把自己的方法寫出來，把卡住的地方標清，明天問老師，週四晚上補好。若還不能確定，我會在說明上留一句“這裏待確認”，不會把猜測寫成已經覈對的結論。小禾，請你先整理我已經檢查過的第一道題。</p></div><p class="gloss">例題: worked example</p><p class="gloss">待確認: to be confirmed</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. What is Xiaoning asked to send before Friday?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 自己負責的兩道例題說明</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 全班所有作業的完整答案</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 小博週四訓練後的照片</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. What should Xiaohe prepare for Xiaobo’s Friday check if the second method is still uncertain?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 刪去待確認提示，把猜測當成正確方法發佈</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 要求小博週四取消訓練替小寧寫兩道題</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 已覈對的一題，以及另一題待確認的標記</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">我對社區裏的小花園很感興趣，但還不確定以後想學什麼。本月我先每週觀察同一處花園，記下光照和植物變化，再向照顧花園的鄰居請教。月底有一次興趣交流，我想帶着記錄去聽不同人的經驗，而不是現在就決定未來的工作。媽媽說，先把一個問題看清楚，也是準備。</p></div><p class="gloss">光照: light conditions</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What is the writer’s immediate preparation for the interest exchange?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 持續觀察一處花園，記變化並請教鄰居</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 立刻選定未來職業，不再比較其他興趣</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 月底以前買下社區裏的全部植物</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">興趣體驗公告：甲是週六上午的植物觀察，需帶連續三天的觀察記錄；週五中午前登記，免費。乙是週日下午的聲音故事製作，不用帶樂器，但須在週四前交一段自己錄的生活聲音；材料費十五元。兩項都由社區老師帶領，名額分別確認。<br>小遙給同伴的回覆：我週日上午纔要去看親戚，兩個活動的時間其實都能參加。不過我最想了解葉子在不同光線下的變化，已經記了兩天。我沒有合適的生活錄音，週三和週四晚上還要排練。我準備明天再記一天，再看看甲的登記頁是否還有位置。報名沒確認以前，我不會把週六的名額也答應給朋友。</p></div><p class="gloss">樂器: musical instrument</p><p class="gloss">排練: rehearse</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. Which preparation difference is correctly stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 甲和乙都必須自帶一件樂器</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 甲要觀察記錄，乙要自己錄的生活聲音</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 甲要錄生活聲音，乙要植物觀察記錄</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Why is finishing the notes and checking A’s registration a suitable next step?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲乙恰好與她週日上午探親完全同時</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因爲寫了兩天記錄就已自動取得甲的名額</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 符合她的植物興趣，也能利用已完成的兩天記錄趕上登記</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">讀書會公告：本週五午休交流原創短故事，每組交一頁推薦材料。必須有一段不超過三句的內容簡介和一條選自故事的原句，不要求每個成員都上臺。週四晚八點前發來，老師會提前放到屏幕上。<br>小禾：我想做內容簡介，短一點方便大家先了解故事。我放學後趕車，不能留下來練。小杜：我不太願意站到前面，但可以找一句最能表現人物變化的話，寫下爲什麼選它。小禾：這樣我寫簡介，你選原句和理由。週三晚上先互相看一遍，蘇芸週四午休檢查，再由我晚上七點半發送。小杜：好，朗讀可以請願意的同學負責，不必爲此交換我們已經答應的部分。</p></div><p class="gloss">簡介: brief introduction</p><p class="gloss">原句: original sentence/quotation</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. Why does Xiaohe prefer to prepare the short introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 方便大家先了解故事，也不用放學後留下練習</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 公告規定每位成員都必須上臺朗讀</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 她認爲選取原句比介紹內容更重要</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. Which division and submission plan meets both the notice and the replies?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 小杜只畫封面，不選原句，週五午休再交</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每個人先上臺練完，才由小禾寫簡介</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 小禾寫簡介、小杜選原句，檢查後周四七點半發出</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">這周讀書會推薦原創故事《窗邊的椅子》。故事裏的女孩總把窗邊的位置留給自己，後來發現新來的同學想坐那裏，是爲了看清黑板旁的課程表。這篇短評不替所有讀者下結論，而是請大家找出女孩前後兩次讓座時說的話，比較她的理由。喜歡討論人物想法的同學，可以先讀這篇。</p></div><p class="gloss">讓座: offer a seat</p><p class="gloss">短評: short review</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. What is the main focus of the review?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 公佈所有讀者必須接受的唯一結論</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 教授怎樣畫出窗邊椅子的詳細步驟</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 引導讀者比較人物兩次讓座的理由</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">原創故事《第三把椅子》裏，阿南準備在班級小演出中講一段最長的故事。他覺得說得越多，大家越會記得自己。排練時，小敏很少插話，只在旁邊擺好三把椅子，提醒後來的人從哪裏進場。阿南心想，她做的事情太少，演出時大概沒人會注意。<br>正式演出前，一位同學臨時忘了從哪邊走，小敏用手指了指空着的椅子，他就順利接上了。阿南講完以後，看見觀衆先向小敏點頭。第二天分配新任務，他沒有搶着選最長的一段，而是先問小敏哪一處還需要人幫忙。他仍想講故事，也把自己選的段落提前練好了。</p></div><p class="gloss">排練: rehearse</p><p class="gloss">進場: enter the performance area</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. Which contrast best describes Anan’s changed view?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 原先想講故事，後來拒絕準備任何段落</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 原先只重視說得多，後來也注意到安靜的配合</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 原先認爲演出需要合作，後來只願自己上臺</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. What can reasonably be inferred from the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 他願意把自己的表達與小組需要一起考慮</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 他已經決定有價值的工作都不能說話</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 他認爲只要幫忙就不必練習自己的一段</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">社區花園提案：週日上午八點集合，記錄不同區域澆水前後的情況。大家兩人一組，一人看老師標出的水量，一人記錄。量杯和記錄板由花園提供，自帶水杯只供自己飲水，不能用來量澆花的水。記錄時不要自己增加水量。<br>補充通知：本週入口旁的小路維修，請從西門進入，東門不開。八點到八點十五分先講說明，第一次參加的人須聽完才能開始。小安第一次來，八點前能到，想學習怎樣根據記錄照顧植物。他決定先找一個搭檔，帶好自己的飲水杯，從西門進，聽完說明後再到指定區域，不因爲自己來得早就先給花澆水。</p></div><p class="gloss">量杯: measuring cup</p><p class="gloss">搭檔: partner</p><p class="gloss">水量: amount of water</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. Which equipment does the garden provide for recording?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每個人自己的飲水杯</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 量杯和記錄板</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 用來維修入口小路的全部工具</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which plan satisfies both the original proposal and the update?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 從東門進，用飲水杯先加水再聽說明</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 八點到後獨自隨意加水，省去配對和說明</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 從西門進，聽完說明後與搭檔按標示記錄</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">本週社區花園試用新的記錄表，只記錄週末兩次活動中用了多少澆花的水，不記錄居民家裏的用水。遇到下雨，負責人會先檢查土，再決定那次是否需要澆水，並在表上說明原因。參加者不必爲了讓數字更小而少帶自己的飲用水。試行結束後，大家一起討論記錄表哪裏需要改。</p></div><p class="gloss">試行: trial implementation</p><p class="gloss">居民: residents</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. What is within the scope of this trial?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 檢查所有居民家裏的日常用水並排名</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 記錄週末兩次活動的澆花用水，雨天先判斷是否需要</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 無論是否下雨，兩次活動都必須使用同樣的水量</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小圓的記錄：以前我總把看喜歡的節目放在最後，常常看完纔想起第二天要交的東西。最近兩週，我先檢查第二天的物品，再選一小段節目看。星期三有社團活動，我那天沒看，也記了下來。這兩週有三天早上沒有再回房間找材料，出門前也多出幾分鐘。<br>朋友回覆：你想保留看節目的興趣，又不想臨出門才找東西，可以繼續試試這個順序。要是某天事情多，少看一段或改到週末也可以。小圓補充：我願意再記一週，尤其想看看有社團活動的那天怎樣安排。現在的變化只是我這幾天的感受，不能說所有人照做都會一樣。</p></div><p class="gloss">順序: sequence</p><p class="gloss">補充: add further information</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What change does Xiaoyuan explicitly report?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 兩週裏每天都看了完整的節目</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 有三天早上沒再回房間找材料</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 已經不需要爲第二天準備任何物品</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Why does the friend suggest continuing the sequence with flexible viewing?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲記錄已證明人人都應按完全相同的時間表生活</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因爲只要不看節目，所有出門前的問題都能消失</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 它兼顧她保留興趣和提前準備的需要，也允許忙時調整</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3B-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">去年學做社區節目時，我每天想把整段錄音一次錄好。一處讀錯，就從頭開始，常常做到很晚。第一次播放時還是有一句不太清楚，我很失望。鄰居聽完卻問我能不能繼續介紹街邊的小店，還說他記住了那家店的故事。我才發現，聽衆不只在數我讀錯的地方。<br>今年我還想做節目，但每週只有週二和週六各半小時。我準備把內容分成兩小段，先覈對意思，再分別錄音，最後請同伴聽有沒有關鍵內容漏掉。到約好的時間就先停，不再反覆從頭來。週二結束後，我在本子上寫的是“下次補上店主的回答”，而不是“今晚必須把所有錯誤都改完”。</p></div><p class="gloss">覈對: check against a source</p><p class="gloss">店主: shop owner</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. Which current adjustment is supported by the past problem and available time?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 分段覈對和錄音，在兩次半小時內完成小目標</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 每次有一個讀音出錯就把所有錄音從頭重做</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 不再檢查關鍵內容，只追求錄音時間更長</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. What can reasonably be inferred from the note at the end?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 作者已經決定以後所有內容都交給店主完成</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 作者認爲只要節目有人聽，就完全不必修改</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 作者把下一步變得具體，並不再要求一晚消除所有錯誤</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 25 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 25 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Reply to a reading-group plan</h2><p>Reply to Yao in Chinese. Say whether you can check the plan at Thursday lunchtime. Choose role-reading, a discussion of the characters or another relevant format, and explain why. State which part you can prepare. Offer a feasible adjustment to the missing speaker equipment and ask one relevant clarification or confirmation. About 60-90 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小安：讀書小組週五要介紹我們讀的短故事。你週四午休能來檢查安排嗎？你喜歡分角色朗讀，還是討論人物？你能先準備哪一部分？活動改在普通教室，沒有音箱，原來播放背景錄音的計劃要改。請說說你的想法，也問清你需要知道的事。<br>小遙</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can attend the Thursday lunchtime check.</li><li>Choose a relevant format and give a reason.</li><li>State a preparation task you can take.</li><li>Address the absence of speaker equipment with a feasible adjustment.</li><li>Ask one relevant clarification or confirmation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>An unexpected problem in a shared task</h2><p>Using the fictional activity card, write connected Chinese paragraphs for a classmate about a cooperation problem and how it was handled. Include time and context, at least two actions in sequence, the contrast between your original expectation and the result, a reason or feeling, and a reflection or next step. You may add plausible details consistent with the card. About 140-180 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">虛構經歷卡<br>時間：上個月週日上午<br>任務：兩人在社區花園觀察，一人看、一人記錄<br>原先期待：分好工，很快完成<br>意外：風吹倒水杯，記錄紙溼了，部分內容看不清<br>處理：移開紙；查看同伴的現場照片；請老師一起覈對；不能確認的標明，不能編數字<br>結果：比計劃慢，但交出了說明問題的記錄<br>感受和下一步：自行選擇，與事實一致</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Establish last month’s Sunday morning and a community garden observation task.</li><li>Describe one action from the card.</li><li>Describe a second action in a consistent sequence.</li><li>Contrast the original expectation with the actual result.</li><li>Explain a feeling or reason.</li><li>Give a specific reflection or next step.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Agree on a shared book recommendation</h2><p>Respond in Chinese to four fixed prompts from a classmate about a shared book recommendation. Each file already contains two plays; play it once, then allow 15 seconds to prepare and up to 30 seconds to respond. Use a reason, a past experience, a response to a new time limit and a specific next step. You may invent details. All four responses form one task /8, not an adaptive conversation.</p><p>You and a classmate are preparing a book recommendation for a community reading group. Personal experience may be fictional.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>Express a relevant need or preference.</li><li>Use a past experience to explain it.</li><li>Respond feasibly to the shorter presentation time.</li><li>Give a final arrangement, your next step and a relevant confirmation.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Recommend a community participation plan</h2><p>Recommend one of the two plans to your class. Compare a relevant feature of both, support your choice with two different details from the card, acknowledge a limitation, and propose a practical next step. Either choice can receive full credit if its constraints are handled. Prepare for 60 seconds and speak for up to 120 seconds. This task uses an on-screen card, not an audio question.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">班級情況：12人，週六上午全部有空；其中8人下午也有空。希望大多數同學能參加；材料總預算50元。<br>甲：社區花園觀察，週六9:00–10:00，免費，最多16人；週五12:00前提交名單；室外活動，下雨取消，不移到室內；出門前查看通知。<br>乙：鄰里推薦書單，週六14:00–15:00，室內，最多12人；全組材料費40元；週五18:00前交三本書的簡短介紹並報名，逾時不加人。<br>可以推薦任一方案，但須按實際時間、預算和截止要求說明參與範圍與下一步。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare a relevant feature of both plans.</li><li>Make a clear recommendation.</li><li>Use one supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Use a different supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Identify a limitation of the chosen plan.</li><li>Give a next step that addresses the limitation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>